# Visual Editor Markdown Preview 

The live visual editor will need to update the raw plain text in a fast manner. This edit is fast and syncing is added as you see with the document.


Pressing enter create a new block. I can change this **block anytime.** 


## Text Formatting

In markdown, you can use single asterisk or single underscore for *italic*,  double
asterisk for **bold** or double underscore, and single backtics for `inline code`.

- **Bold text**: `**Bold text**`
  
  - __Bold__ : ``__bold__``
  
- *Italic*: `*italic*` or
  - _italic_: `_italic_`
- Inline code `code`: \`code\`
- ***bold italic***  : `***bold italic***`
- ~~strikethrough~~ `~~strikethrough~~` (not in vanilla Markdown but supported by many tools)


## Myst restructext flavor of Markdown

:::{card}

A card admonition from myst

:::

:::{note}

A note style from myst 

:::

:::{code-block} Python


print ("Hello World")

for i in range(1,10):
    do_something_with(i)
:::

## **Github** {underline}`Markdown` {style}`Flavor <color=#1a7f37 mark=#cde7ff>`

Certain style works well in the title above in the visual editor, but in the Nootropy parser it will need some handling.


[!NOTE] 💡
Use Note for general context, links to related docs, or anything informational. 

[!TIP] ✅ Use Tip for shortcuts, optimizations, or the "you probably also want…" hint. 

[!IMPORTANT] 📌 Use Important when the reader needs to know this before they act on the rest of the doc.

[!WARNING] ⚠️ Use Warning for things that will surprise people: breaking changes, side effects, footguns. 

[!CAUTION] 🛑 Use Caution for the dangerous stuff. Data loss, irreversible operations, security gotchas.

